Electronic lien and title system. 25LSO-0074, 1.0
FISCAL NOTE
FY 2026 FY 2027 FY 2028
NON-ADMINISTRATIVE IMPACT
Anticipated Expenditure increase
HIGHWAY FUND $139,200 $139,200 $0
Source of expenditure increase:
This bill creates a statewide electronic lien and title system to be implemented
and administered by the Department of Transportation (Department). The Department
anticipates it will need to hire two (2) temporary motor vehicle services positions
to provide support for current Department duties while the system is being
developed, resulting in an expenditure increase to the Highway Fund of $139,200 in
FY 2026 and $139,200 in FY 2027.
Assumptions:
The Department assumes the two (2) temporary positions will be designated as FIAC07
positions and budgeted at $5,800 per month for 24 months, the anticipated period
of developing a statewide electronic lien and title system.
The expenditure increase reflected above could be considered an administrative
cost. However, for simplicity and to follow consistent practice on legislation of
this type, it is included on the fiscal note.
